    "updated_at": "2022-09-06T18:51:56Z",
    "body": "refCount check is there to detect any range, selection, and other objects referencing this text node since range & selection changes are observable. It accounts for the existence of JS wrapper in which case refCount would be positive. If the script had created JS wrapper for this node, then it's observable via object identity checks.",
